        {
          "type": "graph",
          "say": "The checkout page sends the card number straight to the card vault, never through the merchant. The vault stores it encrypted, and returns a token. The merchant's server only ever sees that token. To take a payment, it calls the payment service with the token. When the charge must reach the card network, the vault swaps the token back for the card, inside its own boundary. So only the vault is in PCI scope. Everything else handles tokens that are useless to a thief.",
