    {
      "id": "03",
      "title": "Reliable webhooks",
      "question": "How do you reliably notify a merchant that a payment succeeded?",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "type": "question",
          "say": "Question three. How do you reliably notify a merchant that a payment succeeded, even when their server is down? Pause and answer out loud.",
          "pauseAfter": 3,
          "props": {
            "question": "How do you <em>reliably</em> tell a merchant a payment succeeded?"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "graph",
          "say": "When a charge succeeds, the payment service writes an event, in the same transaction as the charge, and puts it on a durable queue. A webhook worker posts the event to the merchant's endpoint. If the endpoint fails, or times out, the worker retries with exponential backoff: after one minute, then five, then thirty, for up to three days. Delivery is at least once, so the merchant must deduplicate by event ID. And every event stays in a log, so merchants can reconcile anything they missed.",
          "props": {
            "title": "Retry until <em>acknowledged</em>",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "id": "pay",
                "label": "Payment\nservice",
                "x": 220,
                "y": 410,
                "w": 230,
                "h": 90
              },
              {
                "id": "queue",
                "label": "Durable queue",
                "x": 640,
                "y": 410,
                "w": 250,
                "h": 70
              },
              {
                "id": "worker",
                "label": "Webhook\nworker",
                "x": 1070,
                "y": 410,
                "w": 230,
                "h": 90
              },
              {
                "id": "merchant",
                "label": "Merchant\nendpoint",
                "x": 1560,
                "y": 410,
                "w": 250,
                "h": 90
              },
              {
                "id": "log",
                "label": "Event log",
                "x": 900,
                "y": 650,
                "w": 250,
                "h": 70
              }
            ],
            "edges": [
              {
                "from": "pay",
                "to": "log"
              },
              {
                "from": "pay",
                "to": "queue",
                "w": "evt_9"
              },
              {
                "from": "queue",
                "to": "worker"
              },
              {
                "from": "worker",
                "to": "merchant",
                "w": "POST evt_9"
              }
            ],
            "panels": [],
            "steps": [
              {
                "at": "writes",
                "nodes": {
                  "pay": "active",
                  "log": "active"
                },
                "edges": {
                  "pay-log": "relax"
                },
                "note": "Write the event with the charge, atomically"
              },
              {
                "at": "durable",
                "nodes": {
                  "log": "base",
                  "queue": "active"
                },
                "edges": {
                  "pay-log": "base",
                  "pay-queue": "relax"
                },
                "note": "Enqueue it durably"
              },
              {
                "at": "posts",
                "nodes": {
                  "pay": "base",
                  "queue": "base",
                  "worker": "active"
                },
                "edges": {
                  "pay-queue": "base",
                  "queue-worker": "relax",
                  "worker-merchant": "relax"
                },
                "note": "Worker POSTs evt_9 to the merchant"
              },
              {
                "at": "fails",
                "nodes": {
                  "merchant": "dim"
                },
                "edges": {
                  "queue-worker": "base",
                  "worker-merchant": "dim"
                },
                "note": "500 or timeout: not delivered"
              },
              {
                "at": "backoff",
                "nodes": {
                  "worker": "queued"
                },
                "note": "Retry after 1 min, 5 min, 30 min … up to 3 days"
              },
              {
                "at": "once",
                "nodes": {
                  "worker": "base",
                  "merchant": "done"
                },
                "edges": {
                  "worker-merchant": "tree"
                },
                "note": "At least once: dedupe on the event ID"
              },
              {
                "at": "reconcile",
                "add": [
                  {
                    "from": "merchant",
                    "to": "log",
                    "w": "GET /events"
                  }
                ],
                "nodes": {
                  "log": "active"
                },
                "edges": {
                  "merchant-log": "relax"
                },
                "note": "Missed something? Re-fetch from the event log"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "say": "On the merchant's side, verify the signature first, so you know the event really came from the gateway. If you have already processed this event ID, acknowledge it, and do nothing. Otherwise, do the work and record the ID, in one transaction. And return two hundred quickly, or the gateway keeps retrying.",
          "props": {
            "title": "The merchant <em>dedupes</em>",
            "file": "webhooks.py",
            "tag": "merchant side",
            "lang": "python",
            "size": 23,
            "width": 1120,
            "code": "def handle_webhook(request):\n    event = verify_and_parse(request)        # check the signature\n    if processed.exists(event.id):\n        return 200                           # duplicate: ack, do nothing\n    with db.transaction():\n        fulfil_order(event.data)\n        processed.insert(event.id)\n    return 200                               # ack fast, retries stop",
            "highlights": [
              {
                "at": "signature",
                "lines": "2",
                "note": "Reject forged events"
              },
              {
                "at": "already",
                "lines": "3-4",
                "note": "Seen this ID? Ack and skip"
              },
              {
                "at": "transaction",
                "lines": "5-7",
                "note": "Work + record ID atomically"
              },
              {
                "at": "quickly",
                "lines": "8",
                "note": "A 2xx stops the retries"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
